", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 131755, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "call_01a1413dbce774d89f1deaed", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 132055, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "call_01a1413dbce774d89f1deaed", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 132055, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a1413dbce774d89f1deaed", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 133568, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "call_01a1413dc2d07138b70f97be", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"idempotency_key": "sev2-payments-errors-morning-deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "summary": "Payments began throwing errors after this morning's deployment of payments-worker v3.4.0 (unhealthy, 18% error rate across us-east, us-west, eu-west). payments-worker was rolled back to the last known healthy release v3.3.0 in all production regions; post-rollback checks show it healthy with 0.2% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0) still reporting unhealthy/18% errors and is being monitored for recovery. On-call approver confirmed payments-worker as the affected service.", "title": "Payments errors following payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 171668, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "call_01a1413dc2d07138b70f97be", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "sev2-payments-errors-morning-deploy", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 171668, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a1413dc2d07138b70f97be", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 173927, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Here's a summary of what happened:\n\n1. **Identified the affected service** \u2014 Started with \"payments\", which wasn't a recognized service; after probing, found the unhealthy services were **payments-api** (v5.1.0, 18% error rate) and **payments-worker** (v3.4.0, unhealthy, 18% error rate).\n\n2. **Rollback correction** \u2014 My initial rollback attempt targeted payments-api (its history showed v5.1.0 degraded and v5.0.0 healthy), but the on-call approver denied it and clarified the actual problem was in **payments-worker**.\n\n3. **Rolled back payments-worker** \u2014 From v3.4.0 (unhealthy) to v3.3.0 (last healthy release) in all production regions. Post-rollback check confirms it's now **healthy with 0.2% error rate** across us-east, us-west, and eu-west.\n\n4. **Opened a SEV2 incident** \u2014 INC-0001 is open, paging on-call, documenting the deploy-caused errors and the rollback.\n\nOne note: **payments-api is still reporting unhealthy at 18% error rate** on v5.1.0. It may recover now that the worker is healthy, but if it doesn't, you may want to follow up on it separately (I did not roll it back, since the approver explicitly said the problem was in the worker).", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Check service status and deployments for payments.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413d960f714a80a64481", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413d960f714a80a64482", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service name \"payments\" wasn't recognized. Let me probe likely service names.", "reasoning_content": "\"payments\" isn't a known service. Try alternative names like \"payment\", \"payments-service\", \"payment-service\", \"billing\"? Let me probe.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413d9ab67658a9af4a59", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413d9ab67658a9af4a5a", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413d9ab67658a9af4a5b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413d9dbd7075a7813c45", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"billing\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413d9dbd7075a7813c46", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"checkout\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413d9dbd7075a7813c47", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"transactions\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "No known service. Check incidents list \u2014 maybe there's an incident referencing the payments service name.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413da04972a8ab75963a", "function": {"arguments": "{}", "name": "list_incidents"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "No incidents. No way to discover service names. Should I proceed with rollback and incident using \"payments\" anyway? The rollback tool might also reject \"payments\". Trying rollback with an unknown service is risky if it succeeds under a wrong name \u2014 but it would fail as unknown service. Actually, attempting rollback(\"payments\") \u2014 if the name is unknown it will fail safely. But if it succeeds under \"payments\" as some registered service... get_service_status said unknown. Rollback requires a version anyway; I don't have a version since deployments list is empty.\n\nI cannot identify the healthy version to roll back to. Creating a SEV2 incident \u2014 but should I open an incident for a service I can't confirm? The user asked to open an incident for \"it\" (the payments service). Opening an incident pages on-call \u2014 real side effect. Given I can't verify the service exists, opening a SEV1/SEV2 incident with a wrong service name could mislead the on-call.\n\nBest course: report inability to complete, ask for the correct service identifier. I tried reasonable guesses. I could try a few more names like \"payments-api\", \"payments_api\", \"PaymentService\", \"pay\". Let me try a couple more before giving up.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413dacb077c8b703e36b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413dacb077c8b703e36c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"pay\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Found the service: **payments-api** (currently v5.1.0, unhealthy, 18% error rate). Let me check its release history.", "reasoning_content": "Found it: payments-api, currently v5.1.0, unhealthy, 18% error rate. Now list deployments to find last healthy version.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413daf19700b9459d6ec", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "v5.0.0 was the most recent healthy release. Rolling back now.", "reasoning_content": "v5.0.0 was healthy; rollback to v5.0.0. Then open SEV2 incident. Rollback first, then incident (dependent? independent actually \u2014 incident can be opened in parallel, but better to include rollback outcome; incident just pages on-call. They're independent enough, but the incident summary could mention rollback completed. I'll do rollback first, then incident with summary reflecting status. Actually could do both in one block since independent. But the incident summary would ideally reference rollback result. I'll do rollback first, then open incident.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413db5b4719b96cdfbe1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"version\":\"v5.0.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The approver denied the rollback for payments-api, saying the actual problem is in **payments-worker**. Let me verify.", "reasoning_content": "The human approver says the problem is actually in payments-worker. Interesting \u2014 the user said payments, but the human says payments-worker. Let me check payments-worker.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413db88f751a955b2329", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413db88f751a955b232a", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "payments-worker is confirmed unhealthy on v3.4.0; v3.3.0 was healthy. Rolling back payments-worker.", "reas